WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.160
Fans of the Fast and Furious franchise&nbsp;
will no doubt be very familiar with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.720
ongoing feud between Vin&nbsp;
Diesel and Dwayne Johnson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.200
The Rock entered the series in Fast Five as&nbsp;
Luke Hobbs, a DSS bounty hunter tasked with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.160
tracking down Diesel's character,&nbsp;
Dominic Toretto, and his allies.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.080
"I don't have friends. I got family."

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.040
Hobbs and Dom go from enemies to&nbsp;
frenemies by the end of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.480
and Johnson would go on to appear in&nbsp;
three more films in the main franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.680
But things apparently weren't&nbsp;
always rosy behind the scenes.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.840
While the eighth film was shooting in 2016,&nbsp;
Johnson took to his Instagram to spill the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.560
tea regarding some previous on-set drama. The&nbsp;
actor praised his female co-stars but mentioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.960
the men were, in his words, "a different story."&nbsp;
While Johnson didn't specifically name the acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.440
partners who caused him problems, it was clear&nbsp;
enough that Diesel was the issue. Johnson wrote:

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.440
"Some conduct themselves as stand up men&nbsp;
and true professionals, while others don't.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.880
The ones that don't are too chicken&nbsp;
s--t to do anything about it anyway."

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.080
Since then, the two actors' feud&nbsp;
has been a non-stop back and forth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.840
Johnson was the last to mention it during&nbsp;
an interview with THR in July, in which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.760
wished the franchise well — and confirmed&nbsp;
he wouldn't appear in any more Fast films.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.280
"I'll see you soon."
"...No you won't."

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.800
However, it seems like Diesel is&nbsp;
bringing up their rivalry yet again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.360
albeit in a totally surprising way. In&nbsp;
an Instagram post shared on November 7th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.680
Diesel offered the olive branch of all olive&nbsp;
branches to his former co-star. He wrote:

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.160
"My little brother Dwayne... the time has&nbsp;
come. The world awaits the finale of Fast 10.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.240
As you know, my children refer to you as Uncle&nbsp;
Dwayne in my house. There is not a holiday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.360
that goes by that they and you don't send well&nbsp;
wishes... but the time has come. Legacy awaits."

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.320
Of course, not only is Fast 10 on its way, but so&nbsp;
is Fast 11, with both films serving as a two-part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.440
epic finale for the long-running series. Referring&nbsp;
to the late Paul Walker, Diesel continued:

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.560
"I told you years ago that I was&nbsp;
going to fulfill my promise to Pablo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.720
I swore that we would reach and manifest&nbsp;
the best Fast in the finale that is 10!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.240
I say this out of love... but you must&nbsp;
show up [...] Hobbs can't be played by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.000
no other. I hope that you rise to the&nbsp;
occasion and fulfill your destiny."

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.960
So it looks like Diesel is happy&nbsp;
to let bygones be bygones for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.320
sake of the Fast franchise. But&nbsp;
will Johnson feel the same way?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.480
Well, right now Johnson has yet to respond to&nbsp;
his former co-star's plea for reconciliation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.520
But considering how active he is on social media,&nbsp;
you can probably expect to hear something soon.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.280
It's worth noting that, even before his new&nbsp;
Instagram post, Diesel appeared to be over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.120
their feud. In a June interview with Men's&nbsp;
Health, the actor claimed his issues with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.280
Johnson came from pushing his co-star to the&nbsp;
limit to get the best performance. He said:

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.760
"That took a lot of work. We&nbsp;
had to get there, and sometimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.640
at that time, I could give a lot&nbsp;
of tough love. Not Felliniesque,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.800
but I would do anything I'd have to do in order&nbsp;
to get performances in anything I'm producing."

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.640
Nevertheless, it's probably going to take a&nbsp;
lot more than an Instagram plea to get Dwayne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.040
Johnson signed on to Fast 10 and 11. And there's&nbsp;
no way to know if Vin Diesel has reached out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.760
Johnson in private, or whether the social media&nbsp;
strategy is currently his only plan of action.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.360
Unsurprisingly, if the Fast and the Furious&nbsp;
fandom had anything to say about it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.920
Johnson would have signed on the dotted line right&nbsp;
away. Diesel's Instagram post was liked well over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.960
a half a million times and had 10,000 comments&nbsp;
just a mere two hours after it was posted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.080
In the past, fans seemed to have&nbsp;
taken Johnson's side in the feud,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.920
but for the sake of Fast 10, it looks&nbsp;
like everyone is on the side of family.

